# Epochgram changelog

## [1.8.2] - 2026-07-27
- Fixed What's New startup selection: once a newer version page has already been shown, older pages are no longer auto-shown.

## [1.8.1] - 2026-07-24
- Removed `!important` from invalid URL input style by increasing selector specificity.

## [1.8.0] - 2026-07-24
- Added Calendar sync support for ICS feeds.
- Fixed: pin fly animation, **⌘ Epochgram: Review all**.
- Improved record ordering for the same day.
- Updated README, what's new.

## [1.7.2] - 2026-07-23
- Fixed What's New startup fallback so existing users still see the latest available unseen page when current release notes page is absent.
- Updated What's New decision tests to cover fallback and future-version guard behavior.
- Refined 1.7.0 What's New content wording.

## [1.7.1] - 2026-07-23
- Fixed pin badge mobile shape regression and restored consistent badge silhouette across devices.
- Refined badge hover rendering to reduce seam/text-shift artifacts.
- Hardened transitive dependency security with targeted overrides and lockfile updates.
- Fixed an empty block statement in plugin lifecycle startup handling.

## [1.7.0] - 2026-07-23
- Added pin modes (`today`, `date`, `dock`) with improved pin badge interactions, including touch and drag behavior updates.
- Moved pin and mark state into note YAML frontmatter, including explicit mark hex colors for consistent visible state.
- Added AI bridge opening in the right side-bar webviewer and improved AI bridge stability.
- Improved search and UI consistency with better recent-note suggestion priority and settings wording refinements.
- Updated badge visuals and refreshed the What's New page for 1.7.0 with release illustrations.

## [1.6.1] - 2026-07-12
- Added fallback handling for AI bridge disconnect when closing the Obsidian Web viewer tab.
- Fixed AI bridge server HTTP module loading path via `require("http")` for desktop runtime.

## [1.6.0] - 2026-07-12
- Added cloud backend support for AI bridge summarization and updated related runtime/polyfill flow.
- Added and refined opening AI bridge in Obsidian Web viewer, including startup/open behavior updates.
- Refactored AI bridge settings/validation paths and updated README wording/documentation.

## [1.5.9] - 2026-07-09
- Stabilized startup timeline snap positioning to eliminate micro-jitter on Obsidian startup.
- Preserved world-anchor alignment during canvas resize/reposition.
- Unified date targeting to choose records nearest to Today for recurring/non-recurring entries.

## [1.5.7] - 2026-07-08
- Fixed review-state synchronization for recurring records/context menus, reset reviewed -> draft on real edits, and updated defaults (anchor mdate ON, first Pro title threshold = 1.0).

## [1.5.6] - 2026-07-07
- Fixed review-state persistence so Review all remains stable after reload.
- Extended Review/Draft/Hide propagation to recurring synthetic records.
- Updated file and folder context-menu Review/Draft/Hide actions to apply recurring state updates consistently.

## [1.5.5] - 2026-07-04
- Fixed icon sizing.

## [1.5.4] - 2026-07-04
- Fixed AI Bridge startup fallback and improved settings DOM element creation stability.
- Cleaned up AI Bridge module loading and removed obsolete module-name normalization.
- Improved AI bridge startup state handling to avoid stale bridge references on startup failures.
- Fixed multiple lint warning issues across the codebase.
- Improved N+ badge rendering and platform detection behavior.

## [1.5.3] - 2026-07-03
- Added compact (+n) record click/tap cycling behavior and reset logic when active file changes.

## [1.5.2] - 2026-07-02
- Added `$current` search filtering for the active file and updated search suggestion actions to lowercase.
- Added folder explorer actions for Review, Draft, and Hide; removed the obsolete file-level Show action.

## [1.5.1] - 2026-07-02
- Renamed the **Anchor by mdate** setting label to **Anchor mdate** across UI and docs.
- Renamed **Search results** setting label to **Search results count** for clarity.
- Added a total downloads badge to the README release header.

## [1.5.0] - 2026-07-01
- Refactored a large number of lint warnings and errors, including UI label casing updates.
- Fixed two-digit year parsing and date format positioning issues.
- Added a **Search results** slider to control suggestion count.
- Expanded search behavior to work across all files with query-aware filtering.
- Added same-folder similarity via **Title threshold = 1.0** and updated record/search ordering by modified date.

## [1.4.20] - 2026-06-17
- Fixed lint warning issues across plugin.
- Improved popout window compatibility by using window/activeDocument-safe APIs.
- Updated production build/deploy script behavior and release metadata synchronization.

## [1.4.19] - 2026-06-05
- Metadata-only patch release (version/changelog sync).

## [1.4.18] - 2026-06-05
- Increased today distance indicator opacity for improved timeline visibility.

## [1.4.17] - 2026-06-02
- Fix: AI bridge auto-start after Pro activation/validation when AI features are enabled.

## [1.4.16] - 2026-05-31
- Drafts filter state: session-only (no persistence in data.json).

## [1.4.15] - 2026-05-24
- Remove legacy compatibility shims; enforce canonical alias handling in search/bridge flows.
- Stop mirroring explicit topics to `epochgram-topics.json`.

## [1.4.14] - 2026-05-21
- Timeline viewport: updated bounds to 1000...2100 years.
- Progress bar: updated wording.

## [1.4.13] - 2026-05-20
- Updated README hero/content and examples.
- Stopped timeline inertia when collapsing sidebar on mobile swipe.
- Prevented timeline pan/scroll during dominant right-swipe collapse gestures on mobile.

## [1.4.12] - 2026-05-20
- Fixed blinking state for AI summaries.
- Added more README examples.
- Added/updated tests.

## [1.4.11] - 2026-05-19
- Fixed indexing for cached YAML dates and filename dates.
- Added support for full weekday names.
- Renamed Settings labels.
- Updated README.

## [1.4.10] - 2026-05-18
- Fixed disappeared AI summaries after index refresh.
- Fixed Shift/Alt zoom anchoring and fallback behavior, including scroll-nav vs opened-record date handling.

## [1.4.9] - 2026-05-18
- Added **Anchor by mdate** setting: use mtime instead of ctime as the anchor fallback for files with no filename date or YAML date property.
- Fixed hover right-column shift incorrectly triggering when hovering over a single-row record (no neighboring rows at the same Y position).
- Fixed `yamlDateProperty`, `yamlDescriptionProperty`, and `anchorMdate` settings not persisting across reloads.
- Updated AI feature descriptions ("using local Chrome AI" wording).

## [1.4.8] - 2026-05-18
- Updated manifest and README.

## [1.4.7] - 2026-05-18
- Settings UI: renamed frontmatter-related labels for clarity (Anchor property, Summary property, Parse all properties).

## [1.4.6] - 2026-05-17
- Fix settings autofocus behaviour.

## [1.4.5] - 2026-05-17
- Added **Record width limit (%)** setting to control when timeline rows collapse overflow into `(+n)`.
- Reworked settings layout into clearer sections.
- Updated summary rendering/measurement to respect record-width limits at runtime and tuned summary font zoom scaling.
- Improved mobile touch behavior: smoother inertia carry between swipes and right-swipe sidebar collapse handling.
- Improved interactions and README/docs wording.

## [1.4.4] - 2026-05-17
- Fix mobile Epochgram opening in side panel leaf.

## [1.4.3] - 2026-05-16
- Fixed auto-activating view if `Open timeline on startup` is on.

## [1.4.2] - 2026-05-16
- Added handling for Ctrl/Cmd+Enter and Ctrl/Cmd+Click to open matched records in a new tab.

## [1.4.1] - 2026-05-16
- Fixed timeline startup snap alignment so auto-open startup behavior matches manual open behavior.
- Updated plugin/runtime support paths related to trust/device and base64 handling.
- Refined README docs: updated download links and removed leftover comments.

## [1.4.0] - 2026-05-16
- Reworked AI Bridge settings into YAML and improved summarization flow; added `Summarize current file` command.
- Added bridge and epochs fixes.
